    "id": "BasicAnalysis.lem.ivtAverage",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Intermediate Value at the Endpoint Average",
    "content": {
      "snl": "thm-hyp(list-partial(Type.judge(@g,Type.to(Real,Real)),Type.judge(list-partial(@x_1,@x_2),Real),Analysis.isContinuousOn(g,Icc(min-binary(x_1,x_2),max-binary(x_1,x_2)))),Logic.exists-typed(@c,Real,Logic.and(Set.mem(c,Icc(min-binary(x_1,x_2),max-binary(x_1,x_2))),Eq(Type.apply(g,c),Div.div(Add.add(Type.apply(g,x_1),Type.apply(g,x_2)),2)))))",
      "markdown": "A continuous real function assumes the arithmetic mean of its endpoint values at some point between the endpoints."
    },
